From: Squad-Mind <squad-mind@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 09:31:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20diff-context-forwarding=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20prefix-diff=20session=20context=20before=20forwarding=20to?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20CLI?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OpenAI-compatible clients (gateways, agent frameworks) replay the FULL
conversation history on every /v1/chat/completions call. The proxied
CLIs, however, already hold that history in their own resumed session
(--resume / --conversation chaining). Forwarding the whole array every
turn makes the CLI re-ingest an ever-growing transcript: token cost and
latency grow quadratically over a long session.

Mechanism:

- openai-adapter: new hashMessage() — sha1 over a normalized
  {role, content, name, tool_call_id, tool_calls} projection of each
  OpenAI message, giving a stable per-message fingerprint.
- session-manager: each SessionManager keeps forwardedHashes — the
  fingerprint sequence of everything the CLI session has already
  ingested: all input messages shipped so far PLUS the assistant reply
  the CLI produced each turn (committed after a successful response via
  commitForwardedHashes, threaded through the request queue as
  pendingForwardedHashes so single-concurrency serialization keeps the
  bookkeeping race-free).
- On each request, diffAgainstSession() hashes the incoming messages
  and compares the leading entries against forwardedHashes. On an exact
  prefix match, only the new tail is converted (toCliMessage) and piped
  to the CLI, which supplies the older context itself via --resume.
- Full context is re-sent (and the resume id + hash state reset, so the
  CLI starts a fresh session) whenever: no CLI session exists yet, the
  prefix doesn't match (client edited/forked history), or the tail is
  empty (client replayed identical history). LLM_CLI_PROXY_NO_DIFF=1
  disables diffing entirely and restores upstream behavior.

Supporting changes that shipped with the live-tested WIP line:

- buildSpawnArgs(resumeSessionId, opts?) now threads the request model
  and an optional --agent name (new -a/--agent CLI flag, Claude only)
  into the spawned CLI.
- claude: --permission-mode bypassPermissions for squad workspaces,
  optional ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL/ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN passthrough.
- gemini: --skip-trust + --approval-mode auto_edit (Gemini CLI 0.43+
  workspace-trust gate), refreshed model list.
- codex: route through SessionManager/CLI instead of CodexDirectSession
  so codex turns get --resume chaining and prefix-diffing too;
  --skip-git-repo-check for non-repo workspaces; gpt-5.5 models.
- per-request timeout now defaults to 30 min, overridable via
  LLM_CLI_PROXY_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
